The `format` value is validated against the fixed allowlist `supported_explain_formats` in the base `explain_query_prefix` (base/operations.py:662-669) before the MySQL override appends it. The MySQL override calls `super().explain_query_prefix(format, **options)` first, which raises `ValueError` if `format` is not in the allowlist. Therefore the `FORMAT=%s` interpolation only ever receives an allowlisted value (JSON, TEXT, TRADITIONAL). The `EXTENDED` and `TRADITIONAL` strings are constants. No attacker-controlled value reaches the SQL text unbound.

